summary: Fuzz keylime runtime-policy and DSSE envelope parsing (keylime#1139)
description: |
    Fuzzer test for the REST-facing, network-reachable runtime-policy / DSSE
    envelope parsers in keylime, a Tier-1 fuzzing target identified in
    keylime/keylime#1139:

      * ima.verify_runtime_policy()      - REST entry point (verify_sig off):
                                           json.loads, the .get("payload") dict
                                           assumption, DSSE payload b64dec and
                                           attacker-controlled exclude-list regex
      * ima.deserialize_runtime_policy() - unguarded json.loads() + payload shape
      * signing.verify_dsse_envelope()   - unguarded json.loads(), ["signatures"]
                                           indexing, base64 + X.509 cert loading

    These handlers assume a dict-typed top-level JSON object and index/.get()
    into it without guarding the shape, so a hostile scalar/list request body
    ("5", "[]", "null", ...) escapes as an unhandled AttributeError / KeyError /
    TypeError - a verifier-side 500 / DoS - instead of a controlled validation
    error. The test hunts for that shape-confusion class, plus hangs (ReDoS from
    the attacker-controlled exclude list -> CPU DoS) and resource exhaustion.

    Crash policy is STRICT: only each function's documented controlled exception
    (ImaValidationError) or a normal return counts as graceful; any other
    escaping exception is a finding. Against a keylime that still carries the
    open #1139 bugs the test is therefore EXPECTED to report findings and go red
    - it documents them as reproducers - and turns green once keylime guards
    these parsers.

    The test runs in two layers. A deterministic replayer feeds a generated
    corpus of valid and known-adversarial inputs through each parser under a
    wall-clock timeout; this needs only the installed keylime package and runs on
    every platform. When atheris (coverage-guided, libFuzzer-backed) can be
    imported or pip-installed, a bounded coverage-guided campaign is run on top,
    seeded from the same corpus; any reproducer atheris saves fails the test and
    is attached to the results.

    Campaign budgets can be raised for longer local runs via the
    FUZZ_MAX_TOTAL_TIME, FUZZ_TIMEOUT and FUZZ_RSS_MB environment variables.
contact: Karel Srot <ksrot@redhat.com>
component:
  - keylime
test: ./test.sh
framework: beakerlib
tag:
  - fuzzing
require:
  - python3
  - python3-pip
  - python3-cryptography
recommend:
  - keylime
  - clang
  - python3-devel
  # Importing the parsers under test pulls in keylime's own deps (signing.py
  # imports gpg unconditionally, ima.py's import chain pulls lark); listing them
  # keeps the test from failing to import if keylime's dependency chain changes.
  - python3-gpg
  - python3-lark
duration: 12h
enabled: true
id: ca094891-a39a-4282-a51a-6511e322b39a
